---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE, WHATSAPP } from "../../data/site";
---
<BaseLayout title="How to Build an Activewear Brand on a Budget" description="Start your activewear brand with as little as $500. Complete guide to bootstrapping: choosing a niche, finding suppliers, building a store, and getting first sales without investors.">
    <section style="background:var(--color-primary);color:white;">
    <div style="max-width:56rem;margin:0 auto;padding:4rem 1.5rem;text-align:center;">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:0.75rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <span style="font-size:1.5rem;">🚀</span>
        <span style="font-size:0.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--color-accent-light);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.1);padding:0.2rem 0.75rem;border-radius:9999px;">Beginner</span>
        <span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#94a3b8;">11 min read</span>
    </div>
    <h1 style="font-size:2.25rem;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:1rem;">How to Build an Activewear Brand on a Budget</h1>
    <p style="color:#94a3b8;max-width:42rem;margin:0 auto;">Start your activewear brand with as little as $500. Complete guide to bootstrapping: choosing a niche, finding suppliers, building a store, and getting first sales without investors.</p>
    </div>
    </section>

    <div style="max-width:56rem;margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 1.5rem;">
    <div style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:1rem;padding:2rem;margin-bottom:2rem;">
    
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Start With $500 or Less</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">You do not need thousands to launch an activewear brand. The minimum viable start: $100 for samples (order 2-4 pieces to verify quality), $50 for a domain and basic Shopify theme, $150 for initial ad budget (start with $5/day Instagram or TikTok ads), $200 buffer for unexpected costs. That is $500 total to test your idea before investing more.</p>
    


      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Choose a Narrow Niche First</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Instead of selling generic activewear to everyone, niche down to win. Examples: activewear for pregnant women (modest maternity yoga), activewear for senior fitness (comfort-first designs), activewear for martial artists (reinforced seams for grappling), or curvy activewear (extended sizing with focus on support). A niche attracts dedicated followers and faces less competition.</p>
    


      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Build Your Store in a Weekend</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Use Shopify with a free theme (Dawn or Craft). Set up 5-10 products with product photos from your supplier (most provide these free). Write basic descriptions by adapting supplier product copy. Add an About page and a Contact page with WhatsApp. Launch before you are ready - you can improve everything after you get real customer feedback.</p>
    


      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Get Your First Sale Without Ads</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Post 3 times daily on TikTok and Instagram Reels showing your products in action. Join Facebook groups for your niche and genuinely help people (no spam). Offer a 10% discount to your first 10 customers in exchange for honest reviews. Your first 10 sales will come from content, not ads.</p>
    
    </div>

    <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-bottom:1.25rem;text-align:center;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-wrap" style="<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.75rem;margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
    
      <details class="faq-item" style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">What is the biggest mistake on a budget launch?</span>
          <svg class="faq-arrow"style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;"transition:transform 0.2s ease; fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">Ordering too much inventory before testing. Many new sellers order 200+ pieces of one style, then discover the fit does not work for their market or the color looks different in person. Test with 10-30 pieces first, gather customer feedback, then reorder the confirmed winners.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item" style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">Do I need a trademark to start selling?</span>
          <svg class="faq-arrow"style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;"transition:transform 0.2s ease; fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">No, you can start selling without a trademark. However, file your trademark within your first 3 months (USPTO online filing is $250-350 for one class). You need a trademark to enroll in Amazon Brand Registry, which protects your listings and unlocks enhanced content features.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item" style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">How do I compete with established brands on a budget?</span>
          <svg class="faq-arrow"style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;"transition:transform 0.2s ease; fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">Do not try to beat them on breadth. Beat them on specificity: serve an underserved niche they ignore, ship faster than they do, respond to customers faster, and create content they are too corporate to make. authenticity and speed beat scale in direct-to-consumer.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item" style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">Should I dropship or hold inventory?</span>
          <svg class="faq-arrow"style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;"transition:transform 0.2s ease; fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">For a budget launch, start with dropshipping (order 1-5 pieces per style, have supplier ship directly to your customer). Once you find a winner selling 10+ units per week, switch to holding 2-3 weeks of stock. Dropshipping has lower margins (15-25%) but near-zero risk. Holding inventory gives 40-60% margins but requires capital.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item" style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">How do I handle customer service on a budget?</span>
          <svg class="faq-arrow"style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;"transition:transform 0.2s ease; fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">Use WhatsApp Business app for free (includes automated replies, quick replies, and label organization). Set clear expectations: reply within 24 hours. Create a simple FAQ page to reduce repeat questions. Use a templated response library for common questions. Your personal touch will outcompete big brands even with limited resources.</div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div style="background:var(--color-secondary);border-radius:1.5rem;padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Have More Questions?</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Get personalized answers for your specific business on WhatsApp.</p>
      <a href={WHATSAPP} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;background:var(--color-whatsapp);color:white;padding:0.875rem 2rem;border-radius:9999px;font-weight:700;">Ask on WhatsApp</a>
    </div>
    </div>

    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
        {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is the biggest mistake on a budget launch?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Ordering too much inventory before testing. Many new sellers order 200+ pieces of one style, then discover the fit does not work for their market or the color looks different in person. Test with 10-30 pieces first, gather customer feedback, then reorder the confirmed winners."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Do I need a trademark to start selling?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No, you can start selling without a trademark. However, file your trademark within your first 3 months (USPTO online filing is $250-350 for one class). You need a trademark to enroll in Amazon Brand Registry, which protects your listings and unlocks enhanced content features."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How do I compete with established brands on a budget?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Do not try to beat them on breadth. Beat them on specificity: serve an underserved niche they ignore, ship faster than they do, respond to customers faster, and create content they are too corporate to make. authenticity and speed beat scale in direct-to-consumer."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Should I dropship or hold inventory?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For a budget launch, start with dropshipping (order 1-5 pieces per style, have supplier ship directly to your customer). Once you find a winner selling 10+ units per week, switch to holding 2-3 weeks of stock. Dropshipping has lower margins (15-25%) but near-zero risk. Holding inventory gives 40-60% margins but requires capital."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How do I handle customer service on a budget?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Use WhatsApp Business app for free (includes automated replies, quick replies, and label organization). Set clear expectations: reply within 24 hours. Create a simple FAQ page to reduce repeat questions. Use a templated response library for common questions. Your personal touch will outcompete big brands even with limited resources."
        }
    }
    ],
    })} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": SITE.url },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Resources", "item": SITE.url + "/resources" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "How to Build an Activewear Brand on a Budget", "item": SITE.url + "/resources/undefined" },
    ],
    })} />

 <!-- FAQ accordion arrow rotation -->
 <script>
 document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item').forEach(item => {
   const arrow = item.querySelector('.faq-arrow');
   if (arrow) {
     item.addEventListener('toggle', () => {
       arrow.style.transform = item.open ? 'rotate(180deg)' : 'rotate(0deg)';
     });
   }
 });
 </script>
</BaseLayout>